This confirms the analysis: the scaffold never auto-adds an annotation processor, and the deciding factor is whether *test source* defines new Micronaut-annotated types needing compile-time processing (as with sourcegen's code-generating annotations). Since `@Secured`/`@RunAs`/`@CreatedBy`/`@UpdatedBy` are plain reflectable markers with no code-generation or bean-processing requirement, a test can exercise them via ordinary reflection without `micronaut-inject-java`. This validates the earlier decision — no changes needed.

